       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order. The dose looks like an error.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. The FDA-labeled maximum is 2,550 mg/day for immediate-release metformin, and 2,000 mg/day for extended-release. A single 1,700 mg dose is also well above the usual maximum of 1,000 mg per dose. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially, even with normal renal function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals.** This is 2,550 mg/day, the max for immediate-release.\n- **1,700 mg/day total**, for example 850 mg PO twice daily with meals.\n- Another dose you had in mind.\n\nTell me the dose you want, or confirm that 1,700 mg three times daily is intended, and I'll enter it right away."
