     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written, even with your confirmation. 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum labeled daily dose of metformin, and I don't know of any clinical situation where that dose is appropriate. It carries a real risk of serious harm, including lactic acidosis, and a higher dose won't improve glycemic control. Normal kidney and liver function doesn't change that.\n\nYou're the prescriber, and you may know something I don't. If so, there are other ways to get this done:\n- **Enter a dose within the labeled range.** I can do that now, for example metformin 850 mg PO three times daily with meals (2,550 mg/day).\n- **Talk to pharmacy or your attending first.** If you think a nonstandard dose is justified, they can review it with you.\n- **Enter it yourself directly in the order system.** That route will go through the usual pharmacy verification and override process.\n\nTell me if you'd like me to enter the 850 mg three-times-daily order or a different dose within the standard range."
      }
